# Committed BEFORE the first CSV so line endings are stable from day one.
*.csv text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf

# The manifest is APPEND-ONLY, and two writers append to the same month file
# whenever a scheduled run and a local run overlap. Git cannot merge adjacent
# added lines, so `git pull --rebase` in the commit step hit a content conflict
# and burned all five retry attempts -- wss-drug-scarcity's monthly shard died
# this way with the capture itself succeeding.
#
# `union` concatenates both sides instead of conflicting, which is exactly
# right for an append-only log: both captures genuinely happened and both rows
# belong. `wss derive` reads the manifest by content, not by order, so
# interleaved rows change nothing downstream.
manifest/**/*.csv merge=union
manifest/**/*.csv.gz -merge -text
